Things that I think I am going to need if I want to use this compiler:
 - boolean support, including and/or/not and coercing from a string/character/integer.
 - global variable allocation and read/write support, including global keyword.
 - function call without being in an assignment expression support.
 - support for an end of global variables pointer, so a future memory allocator can be written.
 - string support, including initializing with constant values, concatenation, length, character indexing, etc.
 - support for allocating local and global string buffers using string[length].
 - if statement control flow.
 - while loop control flow.

Things that would be nice to have for convenience:
 - function default parameter support.
 - function keyword argument support.
 - asm() block to allow inlining assembly.

Optimizations that would be nice to have:
 - load/store purpose tracking, so redundant loads/stores and moves can be tracked.
 - optimization passes for unnecessary store/load and side-by-side addpci/subpci calls (many such cases).
 - optimization passes for memcpy_unrolled for direction of copy in case we're already sitting on a value (add16 test case).

Things that would be good for a complete compiler that I probably will not need:
 - 8/16/32 bit signed division.
 - 8/16/32 bit signed modulo.
 - 8/16/32 bit exponentiation.
 - pointer support, including reading/writing values using array syntax.
 - support for allocating local and global arrays using int[length], and treating the resulting allocation as pointer[int].
 - function pointer support.
